Package: spacemissionstudio
Version: @VERSION@
Section: science
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34), libgl1, libegl1, libfontconfig1, libfreetype6, libdbus-1-3, libxkbcommon0,
 libxkbcommon-x11-0, libx11-xcb1, libxcb-cursor0, libxcb-icccm4, libxcb-image0, libxcb-keysyms1,
 libxcb-randr0, libxcb-render-util0, libxcb-shape0, libxcb-xfixes0, libxcb-xkb1, libxkbfile1, libnss3,
 libxcomposite1, libxdamage1, libxrandr2, libxtst6, libasound2t64 | libasound2
Maintainer: SpaceMissionStudio contributors <spacemissionstudio@example.invalid>
Homepage: https://github.com/0h3xn4/basilisk-SpaceMissionStudio
Description: GUI mission-analysis application built on Basilisk
 A standalone, GUI-based mission-analysis application for spacecraft
 mission design, using the Basilisk astrodynamics framework (AVS Lab,
 University of Colorado Boulder) as its sole simulation/dynamics engine.
 .
 Self-contained: the package carries its own Python 3.14 with Basilisk
 2.12.0, PySide6 and every other Python package the tool uses, plus the
 SPICE kernels, gravity fields and Earth orientation files runs read. It
 needs no system Python and no internet to install. The libraries it
 depends on are the X11, OpenGL and font libraries of a desktop system,
 which Qt loads from the system.
